 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t a reliable single “best” roofer for everyone, but **Cenco Roofing** looks like a strong first company to get a quote from: the available results report a **4.9/5 rating from 843 reviews**, more than 13 years in Denver, and hail-damage inspection and repair services.\n\nI’d also compare bids from **Metro City Roofing** (BBB-accredited, A+ rating, hail and storm repair) and **Woodberg Roofing & Restoration** (BBB-accredited, A+ rating, storm-damage and insurance-claim support). Those credentials are useful signals, not guarantees—check recent independent reviews and confirm licensing and insurance before signing.\n\nGet at least three written inspections and estimates. Ask each roofer to document the damage, spell out the repair scope and warranty, and explain any insurance-claim assistance. Don’t sign over your insurance benefits or feel pressured to sign on the spot.",
